WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:07.320
Mr. Pendleton's house looked quite different from the last time Pollyanna was there.

2
00:00:07.321 --> 00:00:13.408
Every window was open, and the doctor's carriage was outside.

3
00:00:13.409 --> 00:00:19.313
Leaving her stew in the kitchen, Pollyanna followed a maid down the hall.

4
00:00:19.314 --> 00:00:26.973
They passed Dr. Chilton and a male nurse, who was surprised Dr. Chilton was permitting a visitor.

5
00:00:26.974 --> 00:00:32.189
"I thought Mr. Pendleton didn't want visitors," the nurse said to Dr. Chilton.

6
00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:36.225
"If anyone can improve his mood, it's that child."

7
00:00:36.226 --> 00:00:38.488
"Who is she?"

8
00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:41.218
The doctor hesitated.

9
00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:45.349
"Pollyanna Whittier is the niece of a prominent Beldingsville resident.

10
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:49.378
I don't know Pollyanna well, but many of my patients do.

11
00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:52.692
She does them more good than some medicines!"

12
00:00:52.693 --> 00:00:57.686
The nurse smiled. "What's her secret ingredient?"

13
00:00:57.687 --> 00:01:00.913
"An overwhelming gladness about everything.

14
00:01:00.914 --> 00:01:06.982
I wish I could prescribe her to all my patients," Dr. Chilton joked.

15
00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:15.089
Meanwhile, as Pollyanna and the maid passed the library, Pollyanna noticed how clean it was.

16
00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:19.154
The maid opened a door, and Pollyanna entered a room.

17
00:01:19.155 --> 00:01:22.899
Mr. Pendleton was inside, lying in bed.

18
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:27.798
"I said I didn't want—," Mr. Pendleton began in an angry voice.

19
00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:33.147
"Oh, it's you!" He almost smiled when he spotted Pollyanna.

20
00:01:33.148 --> 00:01:39.338
"I'm so glad to see you!" Pollyanna rushed to his side.

21
00:01:39.339 --> 00:01:44.339
"Well, I'm not glad to be stuck in bed with a broken leg."

22
00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:48.635
"At least you can be glad you didn't break both legs."

23
00:01:48.636 --> 00:01:52.807
"Yes, I'm lucky," the man said sarcastically.

24
00:01:52.808 --> 00:01:57.804
"I should be glad I'm not a centipede with a hundred broken legs."

25
00:01:57.805 --> 00:02:05.939
"Oh, that's a good one!" Pollyanna laughed, and Mr. Pendleton found himself smiling despite himself.

26
00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:09.123
But his mood soon soured again.

27
00:02:09.124 --> 00:02:14.962
"I hate having all these people in my house and needing to pay them too!"

28
00:02:14.963 --> 00:02:19.112
"Yes, Nancy told me you don't like spending money.

29
00:02:19.113 --> 00:02:22.732
I guess you're saving it for orphans overseas."

30
00:02:22.733 --> 00:02:26.105
"What are you talking about? Who's Nancy?"

31
00:02:26.106 --> 00:02:29.272
"Nancy works for my aunt, Polly Harrington.

32
00:02:29.273 --> 00:02:32.523
After my father died, Aunt Polly took me in.

33
00:02:32.524 --> 00:02:37.848
My mother was her sister Jennie."

34
00:02:37.849 --> 00:02:41.642
Mr. Pendleton groaned and closed his eyes.

35
00:02:41.643 --> 00:02:45.580
He looked so upset that Pollyanna was frightened.

36
00:02:45.581 --> 00:02:53.682
"Maybe I should go now," she said. "Enjoy the stew I've brought!"

37
00:02:53.683 --> 00:03:00.018
"Wait!" Mr. Pendleton opened his eyes and gazed fondly at Pollyanna.

38
00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:06.363
"So, you're Miss Polly's niece. I can't believe she sent me stew."

39
00:03:06.364 --> 00:03:10.403
"Oh, no, sir!" Pollyanna said with alarm.

40
00:03:10.404 --> 00:03:14.581
"She said I must be sure not to let you think that."

41
00:03:14.582 --> 00:03:19.007
"Never mind!" the man snapped and turned away.

42
00:03:19.008 --> 00:03:26.124
Pollyanna tiptoed from the room and found Dr. Chilton waiting to offer her a ride home.

43
00:03:26.125 --> 00:03:33.064
"I love to ride!" Pollyanna beamed at the doctor as they drove away.

44
00:03:33.065 --> 00:03:36.467
"From what I've heard, you love most things."

45
00:03:36.468 --> 00:03:43.113
Pollyanna laughed. "That's true, but mostly I love just living.

46
00:03:43.114 --> 00:03:48.205
Of course, Aunt Polly says my days must also be profitable."

47
00:03:48.206 --> 00:03:51.379
"That sounds like something she'd say."

48
00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:57.334
Dr. Chilton looked so sad that Pollyanna wished she could do something for him.

49
00:03:57.335 --> 00:04:02.155
They rode in silence until Pollyanna was almost home.

50
00:04:02.156 --> 00:04:09.339
"Dr. Chilton," Pollyanna finally said, "I think you're in the gladdest business of all."

51
00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.840
The doctor turned to her in surprise.

52
00:04:11.841 --> 00:04:16.669
"How can you say that when I see so many people suffering every day?"

53
00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:20.620
"Because you're helping them, and you're glad to help them.

54
00:04:20.621 --> 00:04:26.064
So that makes you the gladdest person in Beldingsville."

55
00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:30.488
Dr. Chilton looked away as his eyes filled with tears.

56
00:04:30.489 --> 00:04:35.438
He led a lonely life with no wife and no real home.

57
00:04:35.439 --> 00:04:40.637
He lived in his two-room office in a boardinghouse.

58
00:04:40.638 --> 00:04:44.654
But this little girl had made him appreciate his work.

59
00:04:44.655 --> 00:04:46.617
"Thank you for saying that, Pollyanna.

60
00:04:46.618 --> 00:04:50.805
Today the doctor needed some of your medicine too."

61
00:04:50.806 --> 00:04:56.276
"My medicine?" Pollyanna asked.

62
00:04:56.277 --> 00:05:02.797
But they'd arrived at Aunt Polly's, and Dr. Chilton was suddenly eager to be on his way.

63
00:05:02.798 --> 00:05:08.384
Pollyanna found Aunt Polly looking out the sitting room window.

64
00:05:08.385 --> 00:05:13.317
"Why were you in Dr. Chilton's carriage?" she demanded.

65
00:05:13.318 --> 00:05:17.035
"He offered me a ride home from Mr. Pendleton's."

66
00:05:17.036 --> 00:05:21.202
Pollyanna couldn't understand why Aunt Polly was annoyed.

67
00:05:21.203 --> 00:05:24.344
But Pollyanna could try to cheer her up.

68
00:05:24.345 --> 00:05:28.516
"I told Mr. Pendleton you didn't send the stew."

69
00:05:28.517 --> 00:05:31.105
Aunt Polly scolded Pollyanna.

70
00:05:31.106 --> 00:05:35.110
"I said you should be sure he didn't think I sent it.

71
00:05:35.111 --> 00:05:40.877
Which is far different from telling him that I didn't send it."

72
00:05:40.878 --> 00:05:48.834
"I don't see any difference," Pollyanna said as she went to hang up her hat.

